                <pb facs="1361" n="1343" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1343"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.6363/6–346: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-03">June 3, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received June 6—10:42
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–224. Department’s 235, May 24, 7 p.m. Pantepec officials inform me they
                    presented matter to Minister of Finance several days ago pointing out special
                    burden of Decree No. 112 on their company which was materially watered down from
                    previous drafts of letter of protest. Pantepec has not requested any support
                    from Embassy which has consequently made no communication to Venezuelan
                    officials.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
